// home/niri/hosts/unclebeam-pc.kdl — THIS machine's displays.
//
// One file per host, and Nix picks which one gets symlinked to
// ~/.config/niri/host.kdl (home/niri.nix, keyed on
// osConfig.networking.hostName). So config.kdl carries NO hostname branch:
// the other machine's outputs are never even loaded here.
//
// Everything below is a HARDWARE FACT — with one caveat this first round:
// resolutions/scales/positions are measured (carried over from the hyprland
// host file, which read them off this machine), but the output NAME strings
// are DERIVED from hyprland's EDID descriptions, because these panels have
// never run under niri. niri matches the FULL "Make Model Serial" string —
// no prefix matching (unlike hyprland's desc:) — and a string that's even
// one character off silently never matches, leaving the panel on
// auto-config with no error. So on the FIRST niri login run
// `niri msg outputs` and correct the two names below verbatim if they
// differ; the file is an out-of-store symlink and niri live-reloads on
// save, so the fix is one edit, no rebuild.
//
// Physical layout: the Dell sits stacked directly ON TOP of the Alienware,
// both landscape.
//
//   ┌────────────────┐  Dell S2725QS   2560x1440 logical @ 0,-1440
//   └────────────────┘
//   ┌────────────────┐  Alienware AW2725Q  2560x1440 logical @ 0,0  (main)
//   └────────────────┘
//
// `position` is in LOGICAL pixels, i.e. AFTER scale — same rule as
// hyprland. Both panels are 4K (3840x2160) at scale 1.5 => 2560x1440
// logical each, so the top monitor goes at y = -1440, not -2160; using the
// physical height is the classic mistake that leaves a dead 720 px gap the
// cursor has to cross.
//
// Refresh rates are deliberately OMITTED from the modes: given a bare
// resolution niri picks the HIGHEST rate it offers (240 and 120 here) —
// the opposite of hyprland's auto-config, which fell back to the EDID's
// first (60 Hz) mode. Omitting also dodges niri's exact-modeline matching,
// where "@239.99" vs "@239.988" is a silent mismatch.

// Main: Alienware AW2725Q, 27" 4K QD-OLED. 4K240 needs DP 2.1 + DSC — fine
// on this box's RX 9070 XT. on-demand VRR is the hyprland vrr=2
// equivalent: adaptive sync only engages while a window matching the
// variable-refresh-rate window-rule below is visible — games get it, the
// desktop doesn't, so the OLED can't flicker on static content.
output "Dell Inc. AW2725Q 4KTF174" {
    mode "3840x2160"
    scale 1.5
    position x=0 y=0
    variable-refresh-rate on-demand=true
    // Where a fresh login lands (replaces the hyprland workspace-1 pin —
    // niri's workspaces are dynamic and per-monitor, nothing else to pin).
    focus-at-startup
}

// Above: Dell S2725QS, 27" 4K IPS, 120 Hz max. No VRR: it's the
// secondary/reference screen, nothing runs fullscreen on it.
output "Dell Inc. DELL S2725QS 3V7S364" {
    mode "3840x2160"
    scale 1.5
    position x=0 y=-1440
}

// The on-demand VRR trigger for the Alienware: Steam games (every Proton/
// native title gets an app-id of steam_app_<appid> under
// xwayland-satellite) and mpv. Windows matching this rule request the
// variable refresh rate while visible on an on-demand output.
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^steam_app_"#
    match app-id=r#"^mpv$"#
    variable-refresh-rate true
}
